      "usage": "excellency, haughtiness, highness, pride, proudly, swelling.",
      "full": "H1346. gaavah גַּאֲוָה noun feminine majesty, pride (compare Syriac ) — Job 41:7 6 t.; construct גַּאֲוַת Prov 29:23 2 t.; suffix גַּאֲוָתִי Isa 13:3 8 t.; — 1 rising up, swelling of the sea Psa 46:4 . 2 majesty , of Israel Deut 33:29 , Moab Isa 16:6 = Jer 48:29 , scales of crocodile Job 41:7 , of God Deut 33:26 ; Psa 68:35 . 3 pride, haughtiness Psa 10:2 ; 31:19 ; 31:24 ; 36:12 ; 73:6 ; Prov 14:3 ; 29:23 ; Isa 9:8 ; 13:11 ; 25:11 ; גאותי עליזי my proudly exulting ones 13:3 compare Zeph 3:11 .",
